#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097588} :activity/id #uuid "85353624-7ac2-52d1-8562-1afe91b8759a" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048976 :topic/id #uuid "d0827a60-1270-5e75-a5db-1a9836dc00b1" :topic/math-academy-id 1079} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097588 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097791 :tutorial/content "For a particle with position $x(t)$, the **average velocity** of the particle over the time interval $[a,b]$ is given by the average rate of change of position:\n\n$$\nv_{\\textrm{avg}} = \\dfrac{\\Delta x}{\\Delta t} = \\dfrac{x(b) - x(a)}{b-a}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, the **average acceleration** of a particle with velocity $v(t)$ over the time interval $[a,b]$ is given by the average rate of change of velocity:\n\n$$\na_{\\textrm{avg}} = \\dfrac{\\Delta v}{\\Delta t} = \\dfrac{v(b) - v(a)}{b-a}\n$$\n\nTo demonstrate, suppose that a particle moves along a straight line, and its position (in meters) relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by the function\n\n$$\nx(t) = 2t^3\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nt \\geq 0\n$$\n\nis the time measured in seconds. The average velocity of the particle over the time interval $[0,1]$ is\n\n$$\nv_{avg} = \\frac{Δx}{Δt} = (x(1) - x(0))/(1 - 0) = (2(1)^{3} - 2(0)^{3})/(1 - 0) = 2m/s\n$$\n\nLikewise, the velocity is\n\n$$\nv(t) = x'(t) = 6t^2\n$$\n\nso the average acceleration of the particle over the time interval $[0,1]$ is\n\n$$\na_{avg} = \\frac{Δv}{Δt} = (v(1) - v(0))/(1 - 0) = (6(1)^{2} - 6(0)^{2})/(1 - 0) = 6m/s^{2}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "e1c49e4b-7206-5819-b127-c2f562fa1043" :tutorial/math-academy-id 1023 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "defa2861-ea0b-5be8-a72a-4101e1177359" :step/math-academy-id 2011 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097589}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097589 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096717 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096517 :question/id #uuid "924d743e-4984-5d94-84be-381c99697940" :question/math-academy-id "e-571"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7a24f6a-aa0d-576a-a4ff-945335f3301b" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050572} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050901}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097203} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097286}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Average Velocity of a Particle Given Its Position Function"} :step/id #uuid "c2c3e774-0466-5687-8348-ec20933d1013" :step/math-academy-id 2012 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097590}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097590 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096718 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096521 :question/id #uuid "523927ce-8e24-554d-8558-07f51a3d4120" :question/math-academy-id "e-572"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d62ff71-fe48-5612-8f37-bab7cb7f2931" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048713}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097285} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097291}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Average Acceleration of a Particle Given Its Velocity Function"} :step/id #uuid "9c935206-0fc0-512a-9bf5-4f346bee6bcf" :step/math-academy-id 2014 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097591}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097591 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097792 :tutorial/content "So, we now know how to find\n\n- the average *velocity* (given the *position*), and\n- the average *acceleration* (given the *velocity*).\n\nBut what if we are given the *velocity* and asked to find the average *velocity*? That's a bit trickier. However, we can solve this problem by recalling that the average value of a function $v(t)$ over the interval $[t_1,t_2]$ is given by\n\n$$\nv_{\\textrm{avg}} = \\dfrac{1}{t_2-t_1}\\int_{t_1}^{t_2} v(t)\\,\\textrm d t\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "b25ff39d-cfec-5109-8c49-31a8d54ad75d" :tutorial/math-academy-id 1026 :tutorial/title "Calculating Average Velocity Using Integration"} :step/id #uuid "12ea46a3-a7a9-5273-ae68-f843dba89bf3" :step/math-academy-id 2016 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097592}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097592 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096719 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096525 :question/id #uuid "62944da5-875f-542a-9b54-9c3d3c5db947" :question/math-academy-id "e-573"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "803ac4f0-61fe-5efc-b7a5-c73a4235f4bc" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049280}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097293} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097294}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Average Velocity of a Particle Using Integration"} :step/id #uuid "7fa5d198-6f76-58fe-a0de-a2eede2c04f2" :step/math-academy-id 2017 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097676}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097593 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096720 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096526 :question/id #uuid "aa1e2c54-80dc-5e38-a149-c7db63deb418" :question/math-academy-id "e-574"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3046ebca-8a30-5228-a003-b8155cd1a62a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097287} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097292} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527967}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Average Position or Acceleration of a Particle Using Integration"} :step/id #uuid "63d935f4-c3b0-5692-aa00-a8d6bc7db985" :step/math-academy-id 2019} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097676 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097881 :tutorial/content "We can also calculate the average position $x_{\\textrm{avg}}$ and average acceleration $a_{\\textrm{avg}}$ of a particle over an interval $[t_1, t_2]$ using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx_{avg} = \\frac{1}{t_{2} - t_{1}}\\int_{t_{1}}^{t_{2}}x(t)dt; a_{avg} = \\frac{1}{t_{2} - t_{1}}\\int_{t_{1}}^{t_{2}}a(t)dt\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "8e1cdc1f-de87-5b91-9ad0-f2bcab98be3f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5192 :tutorial/title "Calculating Average Position and Acceleration Using Integration"} :step/id #uuid "4f5e263b-c885-5894-bec5-5d0237b91689" :step/math-academy-id 32551 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097593}}] :activity/title "Average Position, Velocity, and Acceleration" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096868}]}
